  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Eu+FyYZC2YHK+vtedzL0nJ6HFQU=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:18.068Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Atabix is a forms-layer specialist in the Dutch Common Ground stack. It works with Open Formulieren and its alternatives, and \u2014 more useful for a screen \u2014 it publishes on the choice between open-source and partner forms, which puts its reasoning about that trade-off on the record rather than leaving it to be elicited in a first call.\n\nA firm that has already argued publicly about open forms has done part of the qualification work in advance. The offsetting facts are that the forms layer is narrow and the record describes the firm as small, so the realistic engagement is depth in one layer rather than breadth across a municipal stack. It sits at priority 3.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Atabix (NL)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Common Ground forms; publishes on choosing open source versus partner forms. \u2014 Forms-layer specialist. Small.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:28:18.068696Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:18.068701Z"
    }
  },
